This is the minimal fix. The import is from the barrel `../helpers/order` which exports `getDispatchLineItemKey` (confirmed in `src/services/helpers/order/index.ts` line 2). The fix matches dispatch line items by both their one-way composite key (no-op, returns raw id) and their return-trip composite key (`id#return`).

## Summary

**Modified file:** `src/services/submit-reservations/apply-report-discounts.service.ts`

**Changes:**
- Added import of `getDispatchLineItemKey` from `../helpers/order`.
- Changed the discount-to-dispatch-line-item match from `lineItem.id === discount.lineItemId` to compare against both `getDispatchLineItemKey(discount.lineItemId)` (one-way) and `getDispatchLineItemKey(discount.lineItemId, true)` (return).

**Effect:** When a promo code is applied to an order containing a return trip, the discount amount is now correctly matched to the return-trip dispatch line item (whose id is composite `id#return`) and the discount propagates into `dispatch.report.price.discount`, so the Mozio email confirmation renders the actual promo-code amount for the return trip instead of a zero/missing value.

No tests were written per the "Tests are NOT your job this turn" instruction. No KB entry written — the fix was a direct application of the prescribed minimal change with no non-obvious pattern discovered.
